{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And when the sun sets, he shall be clean.</b> It is known that וטהר returns to the unclean one, as in וכפר עליה הכהן וטהרה, for there is no mention of day in the verse. Only the Sages translated: even when the sun sets, he may not eat until the stars appear. And they took this verse as an asmakhta, as I explained in the verse לעם נכרי. Therefore they said: טהר יומא [the day's cleanliness]." "<b>For it is his food.</b> His food. I have already explained it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's cross-reference לעם נכרי is unresolved; it may refer to his comment on Genesis or to another passage where he discusses asmakhta similarly."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:41.701216718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}